-- title:
--   Twisted norms in K'ᵥ⊗_{K_v}L_w at unramified places
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $L$, $K'$, $M$ be number fields with $L$, $K'$, $M$ algebras over $K$ and $M$ an algebra over both $L$ and $K'$, compatibly over $K$, and let $L/K$ be Galois. Assume $[M:K']=[L:K]$, that every element of $M$ lies in the $K'$-subalgebra generated by the image of $L$ (so $M$ is a compositum of $K'$ and $L$, linearly disjoint over $K$), that $n:=[L:K]$ is prime and $[K':K]=2$. Let $v$ be a height one prime of $\mathcal O_K$ such that every height one prime $w$ of $\mathcal O_L$ lying under $v$ has $\mathrm{ramificationIdx}'$ equal to $1$ over the prime it lies under. Let $w$ be an element of $v.\mathrm{Extension}\,(\mathcal O_L)$, i.e. a height one prime of $\mathcal O_L$ lying under $v$, assumed to be the unique such, and likewise let $\mathfrak v$ be the unique element of $v.\mathrm{Extension}\,(\mathcal O_{K'})$. Let $\theta$ be a $K_v$-algebra automorphism of the completion $L_w$ of order $n$ whose fixed set is exactly the image of $K_v$ in $L_w$, and assume $[L_w:K_v]=n$. Let $\sigma\neq 1$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ with $\theta$ agreeing with $\sigma$ on the image of $L$ in $L_w$. Finally let $x\in K'_{\mathfrak v}$ be non-zero with $\mathrm{Valued.v}\bigl(N_{K'_{\mathfrak v}/K_v}(x)\bigr)=\mathrm{ofAdd}(n k)$ for some $k\in\mathbb Z$. Then there is a unit $e$ of $K'_{\mathfrak v}\otimes_{K_v}L_w$ such that the product, over $i=0,\dots,n-1$ in order, of the $i$-th iterates of the map $\mathrm{id}\otimes\theta$ applied to $e$ equals $x\otimes 1$.
--
--   This is the completion-level statement that a non-zero element of the quadratic extension $K'_{\mathfrak v}$ of $K_v$ whose norm has valuation divisible by $n$ is a $\theta$-twisted norm from $K'_{\mathfrak v}\otimes_{K_v}L_w$, with $L_w/K_v$ unramified cyclic of prime degree $n$; it rests on the description of norms from unramified local extensions and on the splitting of the tensor product when it fails to be a field. It feeds the construction of twisted norms used in the elliptic case of cyclic base change for $\mathrm{GL}(2)$ in the Langlands–Tunnell input to the argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDedekindDomain_HeightOneSpectrum_exists_units_prod_tensor_map_iterate_eq_tmul_one_of_finrank_dvd_valuation_norm.lean

